Infinite tab freezing (Helium turns InfiniteTabsFreezing on) never freezes a page that holds a live connection: a
WebSocket, WebTransport or WebRTC connection, or a direct socket with a request outstanding, sticky features
included (content::ArdiaFrameHasLiveConnection, from the frame's back/forward cache features). Chrome's freeze drops
a page's WebSocket (DisconnectWebSocketOnBFCache acts on any freeze), so a chat or mail tab left in the background
would lose its connection at every freeze. Every other freezing rule, and the unfreeze interval, is Chrome's.

